From ccd423b99b8d4509163ebc5eedd921ca8962bae7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:31:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-126: the properties grid tested with real input --
 the wheel and Up / Down no longer change a value unasked; the default event
 focused (0.126.0)

A real-input test of the properties panel (DevTools protocol, test/props_realinput.js) found two
silent changes that synthetic events never showed:
- the wheel over a focused number field changed it (Left 54 -> 52, written on leaving): scrolling
  the panel moved the component. The wheel now blurs the field -- the panel scrolls.
- Up / Down on a focused drop-down changed its value and wrote it (Alignment -> taCenter). Now as
  the Object Inspector ("Up/Down Arrow Keys ... select properties"): on a drop-down, a check box or
  a text value they go to the row above / below; Alt+Down opens the list. (A number field keeps
  Blend's +1 / -1; a field with a suggestion list keeps its list.)
Also: the Events button gives the default event's value the focus (EH: "the default event is
selected"); a page (JS) event left blank + Enter / double-clicked when empty = the default name
(as the C++ table); Font.Size's tooltip gives BCB6's point size. The arrow-key scheme of the design
surface stays XAML's (EastSun 20261001 ruling, WPF_DIFF_LOG "not changed").
Tests: props real input (wheel: value kept, nothing sent; drop-down Up / Down: value kept, row
changed; a real double click on Bold = one switch); panels (default event focused, JS default
names). run_all 3/3 layers (lib 168, smoke 198).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
